# REQUIRES: python-api
# The correction for the dispersion of the Python model on the CPU
# (D[python-dispersion]): a pair term's own `dispersion` and an explicit
# correction, against mdir run and the tails of check_pair_tail.py.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/pair_tail_system.py %t 60 60 32 3.7 0.5
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_dispersion.py %t CPU mdir | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: CPU Double cutoff: potential, virial and pressure of default, explicit, term, optout, off equal to mdir run's rows
# CHECK: CPU Double cutoff: the term's energy beyond the cutoff
# CHECK: CPU Double shift: the term's virial beyond the cutoff
# CHECK: CPU Mixed shift: the term's pressure beyond the cutoff
# CHECK: diverges: refused when asked for
# CHECK: no cell, switch: as the control file
# CHECK: tunable exponent: taken by a term left out
# CHECK: python dispersion passed
